<title>EGYPT: Egypt offers controlling stake in housing firm.</title>
<headline>Egypt offers controlling stake in housing firm.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state's Holding National for Construction and Development said on Sunday it would sell to one or more strategic investors a 74 percent stake of its firm Shams Housing and Development ending state control of the company.</p>
<p>The parent company said the deadline for receiving bids to buy 6.2 million shares was September 14.</p>
<p>Bids can be submitted for at least 1.4 million shares. They will be opened on September 15.</p>
<p>-- Cairo Newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
